
  <sn><md>### What is a Plateau?

A plateau is an elevated flat landform

Simple Example

```text
          _____________
         /             \
________/    PLATEAU    \________
       High and relatively flat land
```

There are two kind of plateau
- piedmont
- intermontane


:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-lg-6
#### Piedmont Plateau

A **piedmont plateau** is a high, relatively flat or gently sloping area located **at the foot of mountains**.

```text
      MOUNTAINS
        /\
       /  \
      /    \
_____/      \________
       ↑
  Piedmont Plateau
  (at foot of mountains)
```

**Example:** The **Brazilian Highlands** contain areas associated with piedmont landscapes along mountain margins.

+++ view diagram
![img](https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjNFVjqkI6SI6wUO2Y2on5NwabLTFUUvEaKoFIB3XWAGvkV2M7zwZiDqlaVtthKTIBTivaV5AC_-2X5yntn3JIn_A4B-dqzbW1bRxYAmMXuV8imZ-0b0i5aE0IpLfW7Kk3TgEzSWYAHxUs/s1600/images+%25281%2529.jpg)
+++
:::

:::.col-12 .col-lg-6
#### Intermontane Plateau

An **intermontane plateau** is a plateau **surrounded or enclosed by mountains**.

```text
     MOUNTAINS       MOUNTAINS
        /\               /\
       /  \_____________/  \
      /                    \
      |  INTERMONTANE      |
      |     PLATEAU        |
      \____________________/
```

**Examples:**

* **Altiplano** — Andes, South America
* **Tibetan Plateau** — Asia

+++ view diagram
![img](https://rajras.in/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/image58-1.png)
+++
:::
:::

**Memory trick:**
**Piedmont = mountain foot** 👣
**Intermontane = between mountains** ⛰️ ↔️ ⛰️
