<sn><md>### Patagonia

:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-lg-8
- Southern **Argentina**
- A vast, **dry and cold, step-like plateau** in Patagonia. 
- It slopes generally eastward toward the Atlantic Ocean and is characterized by barren landscapes and strong winds.
:::

:::.col-12 .col-lg-4
![img](https://lakenheathallianceforpeace.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/patagonia.png)
:::
:::
</md></sn><sn><md>### Altiplano

:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-lg-4
![img](https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/dc/Altiplano_map_%28cropped%29_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=original)
:::

:::.col-12 .col-lg-8
- Mainly **Bolivia and Peru**
- A very high **intermontane plateau** in the Andes, lying between major mountain ranges. 
- **Lake Titicaca** is located in its northern part.
:::
:::
